# Air wing and airbase selection, reworked for 2560x1440.
# Overrides eight top-level windows of vanilla interface/airselectionview.gui; the vanilla file stays in place
# and supplies every other window. The untouched vanilla text of each window is in baseline/airselectionview/.
#
# Compared with vanilla:
#   - the selection list holds 20 rows before it scrolls instead of 9. The frame and clipping list that hold
#     the rows are unassigned_airwings_view (frame 582x430 -> 705x964), not air_selection_view.
#   - airbase, wing, gun emplacement and rocket rows are 671 wide instead of 548, on new GFX_1440p_ backgrounds
#   - name and status texts are wider and one font size larger
#   - widgets right of the name moved right by 123
#   - the mission toolbar, the selection toolbar and the list frame form one block: all three end at the same
#     right edge. The mission toolbar keeps its vanilla width of 703 (15 missions x 45 + 2 x 14), which is the
#     narrowest the block can be; the selection toolbar goes from 652 to 703 and the list frame to 705. They touch
#     each other vertically (selection toolbar y 60 -> 51, list y 120 -> 91). The selection toolbar's right-hand
#     group moved by 47, which puts its close button above the close buttons of the wing rows.
#   - the quick deploy popup is 900 high instead of 515, with a one size larger font
guiTypes = {
	containerWindowType = {
		name = "air_selection_view"
		position = {x=0 y=77}
		size = { width=625 height=1056 } # height set in code, but initial value here is used for max allowed height
		Orientation = upper_left
		clipping = no

		containerWindowType = {
			name = "mission_toolbar"
			position = {x=2 y=5}
